Forty five years later, in 2010 the[ Chapel] was suffering from extensive cracking in the[ sanctuary] walls, which was always thought to have been caused by drought. When a gang of cock[ato]os moved into the slate roof and started to destroy it, structural[ engineers] were called in and it was found that the structure had been put at risk by the pillar's removal. For two years the[ chapel] was closed while the pillar was[ reinstated], the slate roof replaced and the interior, including the highly decorative paint work was completely restored.
